From b59be8fcb439c8de8e75cf881b84c83cdd817da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:21:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Admin: add a Guide Coverage tab

Answers one question per vehicle: how many guides should it have, how many
are written, what is left.

THE TARGET IS COMPUTED, NOT HARDCODED

A flat "every vehicle needs N guides" would be wrong in both directions. A
front-wheel-drive car has no separately serviceable differential; an EV has
no oil to change, no spark plugs and no PCV valve. So each job in the
catalog carries an applicability rule and a vehicle's target is the subset
that actually applies to it. The Civic and Escape correctly show a target
of 16 rather than 17 for exactly this reason, and the page says so in its
own subtitle rather than leaving the discrepancy unexplained.

The job catalog mirrors the approved "do cover" list in the coverage-scope
project doc. Adding a row raises the target for every applicable vehicle
and surfaces as newly-missing work, which is intended -- but it should
follow a product decision, and the code says so.

WHAT IS ON THE PAGE

- Five tiles: vehicles, guides built, target, remaining, coverage percent.
  These always describe the whole catalog, never the filtered view. A
  headline number that changes when you filter a table is a number nobody
  can quote.
- Per-vehicle table: target, built, remaining, a progress meter, status,
  and the first few outstanding jobs by name.
- Filters for year, make, model, status and missing-job. The year/make/model
  options narrow against each other so the dropdowns never offer a
  combination that returns nothing. Plain GET form -- no client JS.
- "Biggest gaps" panel: which job is missing on the most vehicles, which is
  the build-order question the report exists to answer. Each row links to
  the filtered view of the vehicles still needing it.

Current reading: 28 built against a target of 100, 28% coverage, biggest
gap is rear brake pads at 6 of 6 vehicles.

GUIDES NOW CARRY A JOB TYPE

RepairGuide gains an optional jobType, backfilled across all 28 guides.
Matching on title was considered and rejected: retitling a guide would
silently stop it counting. Optional so no guide is ever rejected for
lacking it, but a guide without one counts toward nothing -- so the page
lists unclassified guides explicitly instead of quietly ignoring them.

No database work. The report is derived fresh from src/data on every load,
so it cannot drift from the content the way a stored count would. Reuses
guides.view rather than inventing a permission, so every existing role sees
it with no migration.

Verified: rendered against a real Postgres and a seeded super-admin, and
screenshotted at 1500px and 820px -- tiles, filters, meters, badges and the
filtered view all check out, no console or page errors. tsc clean, next
build clean, eslint unchanged at the same 4 pre-existing problems.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
